                <pb facs="0378" n="313" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg313"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/5186: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-02-23T11:00:00+03:00">February 23, 1937—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 24—9 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>54. My 44, February 18, 2 p.m. The Governor sent an officer to the Legation this
                    morning to inform it that the ordinance in question would not be enforced as
                    regards the clause to which I objected.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
